nce", "verb": "CONTAINS", "targetSlug": "niccol-giolfino", "targetName": "Niccolò Giolfino", "context": "Niccolò Giolfino's active period from 1476 to 1555 falls squarely within the High Renaissance, particularly in Northern Italy."}, {"sourceSlug": "niccol-giolfino", "sourceName": "Niccolò Giolfino", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "veronese-school-of-painting", "targetName": "Veronese School of Painting", "context": "Niccolò Giolfino's consistent production of sacred art and distinct style significantly contributed to and influenced the Veronese school of painting throughout the early 16th century."}], "places": [{"name": "Verona, Italy", "role": "Birthplace; Primary artistic center"}, {"name": "Venice, Italy", "role": "Artistic influence"}, {"name": "Milan, Italy", "role": "Artistic influence"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Niccolò Giolfino", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "niccolò-giolfino"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2070123", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Niccol%C3%B2_Giolfino"], "tags": ["Cartographers", "innovation-and-technology", "cultural-diffusion", "temporal-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Niccolò Giolfino left a notable mark on Medieval history, documented across 0 Wikipedia editions worldwide. Key lasting impacts include: Improved cartographic accuracy and geographic understanding; Contributed to synthesis of classical and religious thought informing Renaissance and Reformati.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 6, "significanceNarrative": "Niccolò Giolfino holds significant regional importance as a leading painter of the Veronese school during the High Renaissance, producing a substantial body of sacred art that shaped the visual piety and artistic direction of Verona for decades. His work provides crucial insight into the artistic synthesis of local traditions with broader Italian Renaissance styles.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-11-18T21:13:29Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#44398379393", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Niccolò Giolfino was an Italian painter of the Renaissance period, active mainly in Verona. He painted mainly sacred subjects for local churches.", "newValue": "Niccolò Giolfino (1476–1555) emerged as a prominent Italian painter in Verona during the High Renaissance, a period marked by profound artistic innovation and humanistic rediscovery. Active for over five decades, Giolfino became a pivotal figure in the Veronese school, distinguished by his devout commitment to sacred subjects and his unique synthesis of local tradition with broader Lombard and Venetian stylistic influences. His extensive output for local churches and confraternities solidified his reputation as a master of religious narrative and portraiture, contributing significantly to the visual piety of early 16th-century Verona.

Giolfino’s artistic journey began under the tutelage of Liberale da Verona, whose meticulous detail and vibrant palette profoundly shaped his early style. By the turn of the century, Giolfino had established his own workshop, producing numerous altarpieces, frescoes, and devotional panels. Key works include the 'Madonna and Child with Saints' (c. 1518) for San Bernardino, characterized by its emotional depth and rich color, and the 'St. Peter Enthroned' series (c. 1530s) for San Nazaro e Celso, which showcases his mature command of composition and figure modeling. He was particularly adept at rendering expressive faces and dynamic drapery, often incorporating architectural elements that lent grandeur to his sacred scenes.

Giolfino's legacy lies in his role as a bridge between the Quattrocento traditions of Verona and the burgeoning High Renaissance ideals filtering in from Venice and Milan. His consistent patronage by Veronese religious institutions ensured a steady demand for his art, influencing a generation of local painters, including his own sons. While not achieving the pan-Italian fame of a Titian or Raphael, Giolfino’s oeuvre remains indispensable for understanding the artistic landscape of Verona, providing a detailed visual record of its spiritual and cultural life during a transformative era."}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-18T21:13:29Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#44398379393", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Medieval era: interplay of religious authority, feudal governance, and trade network expansion", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "1476, Verona"}, {"title": "Geographic knowledge gaps and mapping imperatives", "type": "Idea", "year": "1476, Verona"}], "newValue": ["The flourishing artistic environment of 15th-century Verona provided a fertile ground for Giolfino's early training and development.", "The strong demand for sacred art from local churches and confraternities in Verona ensured steady patronage for religious painters like Giolfino.", "The influence of masters like Liberale da Verona and the broader artistic currents of Lombardy and Venice shaped Giolfino's distinct High Renaissance style."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-18T21:13:29Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#44398379393", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Improved cartographic accuracy and geographic understanding", "type": "Idea", "year": "1555"}, {"title": "Contributed to synthesis of classical and religious thought informing Renaissance and Reformati", "type": "Movement", "year": "1555"}], "newValue": ["Niccolò Giolfino's workshop contributed significantly to the visual culture and religious iconography of Verona's churches and chapels.", "His ar